{"title":"Career Roadmap · Marine Research Assistant","role":"Marine Research Assistant","summary":"A Marine Research Assistant supports research on oceans, coastal systems, marine ecosystems, seawater chemistry, marine geology, physical oceanography, climate processes, fisheries, pollution and marine technology. The role can combine field sampling, laboratory analysis, oceanographic observations, GIS/remote sensing, statistics and scientific computing.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Marine Science / Oceanography"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Marine Science / Oceanography → Marine Research Assistant"},{"type":"p","text":"A Marine Research Assistant supports research on oceans, coastal systems, marine ecosystems, seawater chemistry, marine geology, physical oceanography, climate processes, fisheries, pollution and marine technology. The role can combine field sampling, laboratory analysis, oceanographic observations, GIS/remote sensing, statistics and scientific computing."},{"type":"p","text":"This is a strongly aligned entry-level career for B.Sc Marine Science/Oceanography. For independent research and scientist-level positions, an M.Sc/M.S. and often a PhD are the normal progression."},{"type":"h","text":"Career facts"},{"type":"table","header":["Item","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc Marine Science / Oceanography"}],[{"text":"Entry career"},{"text":"Marine Research Assistant"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Ocean Science · Marine Science · Earth & Environmental Science"}],[{"text":"Strongest foundations"},{"text":"Oceanography + marine biology + chemistry + physics + mathematics"}],[{"text":"Important field skills"},{"text":"Sampling, CTD operations, water-quality measurements, field documentation"}],[{"text":"Important digital skills"},{"text":"GIS + remote sensing + Python/R + statistics"}],[{"text":"Research environments"},{"text":"Research vessels, coastal stations, laboratories, universities"}],[{"text":"Long-term route"},{"text":"Research Assistant → Research Associate/Scientist → PhD → Senior Scientist/Research Lead"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Direct alignment","text":"Yes."},{"type":"p","text":"The exact title varies by research institute. Bachelor's graduates may enter as Project Assistant, Research Assistant, Technical Assistant or Research Intern, while scientist and independent research positions generally require postgraduate qualifications."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","What should I focus on?"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build oceanography fundamentals, field/lab skills, statistics, GIS and scientific programming."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Complete M.Sc/M.S. in Oceanography, Marine Science or a related discipline and specialise."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Pursue PhD/research scientist roles and develop expertise in a specific ocean-science problem."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Scientist, Principal Scientist, Research Lead, Marine Consultant or academic leadership."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Physics, chemistry, mathematics and earth-science fundamentals"},{"text":"University + NPTEL"},{"text":"Foundation assignments"},{"text":"Scientific foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Introduction to oceanography and marine biology"},{"text":"University + research papers"},{"text":"Ocean-system mini project"},{"text":"Domain knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Physical, chemical and biological oceanography"},{"text":"University + NPTEL"},{"text":"Oceanographic data analysis"},{"text":"Ocean science"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"GIS, statistics and Python/R"},{"text":"NPTEL + open datasets"},{"text":"Coastal/ocean GIS project"},{"text":"Quantitative skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Marine sampling + remote sensing"},{"text":"Research papers + practical labs"},{"text":"Field/lab project"},{"text":"Field readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Research internship"},{"text":"Marine institute/university"},{"text":"Internship report + recommendation"},{"text":"Research exposure"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Advanced specialisation"},{"text":"Research lab"},{"text":"Dissertation/research project"},{"text":"Research depth"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Research publication/presentation skills"},{"text":"Supervisor + research group"},{"text":"Dissertation + poster/paper"},{"text":"Research readiness"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"If the B.Sc. is a 3-year programme, integrate the Year 4 activities into the final year."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"h","text":"Oceanography"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical Oceanography"},{"text":"Chemical Oceanography"},{"text":"Biological Oceanography"},{"text":"Geological Oceanography"},{"text":"Marine Geophysics"},{"text":"Coastal Oceanography"},{"text":"Estuarine Science"},{"text":"Ocean Circulation"},{"text":"Waves and Tides"},{"text":"Air-Sea Interaction"},{"text":"Ocean-Atmosphere Processes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Marine science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Marine Biology"},{"text":"Marine Ecology"},{"text":"Marine Biodiversity"},{"text":"Marine Microbiology"},{"text":"Fisheries Science"},{"text":"Marine Pollution"},{"text":"Coastal Zone Management"},{"text":"Marine Conservation"},{"text":"Marine Biotechnology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Earth and environmental science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Geology"},{"text":"Sedimentology"},{"text":"Geomorphology"},{"text":"Climatology"},{"text":"Environmental Science"},{"text":"Hydrology"},{"text":"Climate Change"},{"text":